## Smell-Free Pattern ✅

**`ValidateOrder_NullOrder_ThrowsArgumentNullException`** (line 155) is exemplary:
- Uses `Assert.ThrowsException<T>` instead of try/catch
- Single focused assertion on `ParamName`
- No magic numbers, no external dependencies, no control flow

This is the pattern to emulate when remediating the findings above.

