## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Rationale |
|----------|-------|-----|-----------|
| **1** | Assertion-Free Test | Add assertions | Eliminates false-pass risk immediately |
| **2** | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 tests | Uncovers the permanently-hidden branch |
| **3** | Mystery Guest | Inline test data | Unblocks CI — test cannot pass today |
| **4** | Sleepy Test | Await the async call | Removes 2 s of wall-clock waste + flakiness |
| **5** | Exception Handling | Use `Assert.ThrowsException` | One-line change, safer exception typing |
| **6** | Assertion Roulette | Add message parameters | Quick win — clarifies failure output |
| **7** | Magic Number Test | Named constants | Makes pricing intent self-documenting |
| **8** | Sensitive Equality | Assert on properties | Decouples from `ToString()` format |
| **9** | Eager Test | Split or mark Integration | Improves failure diagnosis |
| **10** | General Fixture | Remove `_logger` | Housekeeping — lowest risk |

All smell names above map directly to the **testsmells.org** taxonomy (Peruma et al., *tsDetect*, ESEC/FSE 2020) and are citable in that form.
